@* The wall editor's key bindings, lifted out of KeyboardShortcuts.razor so that page stays under
   the project's file-size rule. Static markup only — content is identical to what the page rendered
   before; the page composes this and KeyboardShortcutsWizard in place of the two sections. *@

    <section class="keyshort-section">
        <h2>Wall editor</h2>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            The editor only claims these keys while you have edit rights on the wall and the editor is in
            edit mode. Each key repeats the gate of the button it mirrors, so a key whose tool is not on
            the toolbar in this configuration simply does nothing.
        </p>

        <h3>Tools</h3>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>a</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Add hold</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>m</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Select / move</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>s</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Shape</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>p</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Paint</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>n</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Name</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>d</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Delete</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>b</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Border (only where the wall border/shape may be edited)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>t</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Tilt (shape tilt)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>u</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Hold usage (only where the page offers the usage view)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>g</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Merge (staged wall updates only, and not during manual alignment)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>k</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Make actual (outside a staged wall update)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>j</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Join duplicate virtual holds — keep one, absorb the other (outside a staged wall update)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>c</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Mark unchanged</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>x</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Mark changed &mdash; flag a hold that was physically swapped, turned or re-set, and
                    with it every boulder still using it (outside a staged wall update)
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>

        <h3>View and actions</h3>
        <dl class="keyshort-list">
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>l</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Toggle hold labels</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>o</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Toggle border / segment outlines</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>i</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Cycle the <strong>missing information</strong> overlay through off &rarr; holds with
                    no colour &rarr; those plus hand holds with no sub-type. Colour is the default,
                    because nothing ever stamps a sub-type: including it badges most hand holds on a
                    mature wall, which is useful for a deliberate pass and noise the rest of the time.
                    Hold type and material are never checked &mdash; every hold gets one by default, so
                    a set value was never necessarily a decision, and neither criterion can tell &ldquo;not
                    filled in yet&rdquo; from &ldquo;deliberately left blank&rdquo;. It is an overlay, not
                    a tool: badged holds stay tappable, so you can fix them in place with <kbd>m</kbd>
                    (Select / move).
                </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>r</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Re-detect holds (where re-detection is offered, and not while one is running)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>1</kbd>&ndash;<kbd>9</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Pick paint colour N from the palette &mdash; <strong>Paint tool only</strong></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>[</kbd> <kbd>]</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Previous / next paint colour (wraps around) &mdash; <strong>Paint tool only</strong></dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>+</kbd> <kbd>-</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Zoom in / out</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>0</kbd></dt>
                <dd>Reset zoom</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <span class="keyshort-plus">+</span> <kbd>S</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Save changes (<kbd>Cmd</kbd> <span class="keyshort-plus">+</span> <kbd>S</kbd> on
                    macOS) &mdash; claimed only while there is actually something to save, and never
                    during a manual alignment. With nothing staged the browser's own Save is left alone.
                </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="keyshort-row">
                <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt>
                <dd>
                    Cancel the active sub-mode and nothing else: naming, a pending merge, a pending
                    &ldquo;make actual&rdquo;, a pending &ldquo;mark unchanged&rdquo;, a pending
                    &ldquo;mark changed&rdquo; or a shape tilt, in that order. With no sub-mode pending the editor does not claim <kbd>Esc</kbd> at all.
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
        <p class="keyshort-note">
            <kbd>Esc</kbd> never discards your unsaved changes. Discarding is a deliberate click on the
            labelled button, because a stray keystroke must not throw away staged hold edits.
        </p>
    </section>
